.TH CHTTPSVR_BOUND_PORT 3 "2026-10-13" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpsvr_bound_port \- report the TCP port that a server listens on
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpserver.h>

ccol_retval_t chttpsvr_bound_port(chttpsvr srv, uint16_t *port_out);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Stores in *port_out the TCP port that the listener of srv is bound
to, in host byte order.  It is the port that the system really bound,
so either the port of the configuration or, for a configuration with
port 0, the ephemeral port that the system picked.  The library reads
it from the socket with getsockname(2) when chttpsvr_start binds it,
the same way the Addr method of a Go net.Listener and the
MHD_DAEMON_INFO_BIND_PORT query of libmicrohttpd report it.

A server started with port 0 binds a new ephemeral port on every
start, so read the port again after a restart.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
srv        The server handle.
port_out   Receives the port.  It receives 0 on every failure.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success        *port_out holds the port.
ccol_invalid_args   srv is CHTTPSVR_INVALID or a stale handle, or
                    port_out is NULL.
ccol_not_permitted  The server does not listen (see
                    chttpsvr_is_running(3)), or it listens on a
                    "unix://" path, which has no port.
.fi
.SH THREAD SAFETY
.nf
Safe to call from any thread while a start or a stop of srv runs.
The answer then describes the listener from one side of that change.
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
chttpsvr_config_t cfg = CHTTPSVR_CONFIG_DEFAULT;
cfg.host = "127.0.0.1";
cfg.port = 0; /* let the system choose a free port */
if (chttpsvr_start(srv, &cfg) == ccol_success) {
  uint16_t port = 0;
  if (chttpsvr_bound_port(srv, &port) == ccol_success)
    printf("listening on http://127.0.0.1:%u/\en", (unsigned)port);
}
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpsvr_start (3),
.BR chttpsvr_bound_address (3),
.BR chttpsvr_is_running (3),
.BR CHTTPSVR_CONFIG_DEFAULT (3)
